@startuml workspace-open
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 17
skinparam shadowing false
hide footbox
title Workspace launch/open — designed, acceptance pending
participant Client
participant "Machine core" as Core
participant Workspace
participant "macOS / app" as Native
Client -> Core: launch app / open web URL / open path
Core -> Core: preflight every root action\nlive admission: both control grants
Core -> Workspace: admitted action
Workspace -> Native: resolve installed app / path / handler\nno launch or consent request
alt missing prerequisite before submission
  Workspace --> Client: DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE\nreason + guidance; no value
else ready
  Workspace -> Native: submit launch/open; request activation\nreuse running copy unless path-constrained
  alt native acknowledgment within wait bound
    Native --> Workspace: accepted application
    Workspace --> Client: AVAILABLE + receipt\noptional observed PID / kernel start only
  else native error, 3 s wait expiry or cancellation
    Workspace --> Client: failed; effect may have begun\nno replay or alternate handler
  end
end
opt receipt includes process and client has desktop:read
  Client -> Core: desktopApplication(process: PID + start)
  Core --> Client: desktop state / absent / classified error
end
note over Client,Native
Installed identity is not a held process or file identity.
Window behavior belongs to the app; later exit remains possible.
Acknowledgment alone does not pass activation acceptance.
Core request deadline may answer first; late results are ignored.
Publication errors can suppress the selected result branch.
Reveal is a separate operation with Finder acknowledgment.
Neither control grant implies read or OS consent.
end note
@enduml
